<title>JAPAN: Mitsubishi Aluminium sees higher 1997/98 sales.</title>
<headline>Mitsubishi Aluminium sees higher 1997/98 sales.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Aluminium Co Ltd said on Thursday it planned a seven percent rise in aluminium sales in the first half of 1997/98 to 14,400 tonnes, despite an expected drop in turnover of extruded products.</p>
<p>Mitsubishi Aluminium said in a statement it expected an eight percent rise in aluminium sheet sales to 12,000 tonnes in the first half of 1997/98 from the year-ago period. It forecast a one percent drop in extruded product sales to 2,400 tonnes.</p>
<p>Mitsubishi Aluminium is 67 percent owned by Mitsubishi Materials Corp.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
